// Texas Grade 4 social studies: Texas history (TEKS 19 TAC §113.15). Every unit is written for Texas. American Indian
// content is light, names groups as the TEKS do (Gulf, Plains, Puebloan and Southeastern cultural regions; Caddo,
// Karankawa, Lipan Apache, Jumano, Comanche) and keeps nothing sacred or ceremonial; the nations that live in Texas
// today (Ysleta del Sur Pueblo, the Alabama-Coushatta Tribe of Texas and the Kickapoo Traditional Tribe of Texas) are
// in the present tense. The missions are told plainly: they harmed many American Indian people. Slavery, secession and
// Reconstruction are factual and neutral.

